1. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method of providing a user with access to a resource of a contact center, comprising the steps of:
(a) providing a search engine interface to a user's computer system for searching documents on one or more websites;
(b) receiving a search query from the user's computer system via said interface;
(c) sending a request based on said search query to a computerised system of a contact center __that is distinct from the search engine system__;
(d) receiving, in response to said request, data enabling a contact center link to be provided to said user, wherein said contact center link, when activated, initiates an interactive communications session between the user and a resource of the contact center __that is selected based on analysis of the search query content and user context__;
(e) returning said contact center link to said user as part of a response to said search query __integrated with document search results__.

2. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 1, further comprising the steps of conducting a search within said documents on one or more websites in response to said search query, and returning at least one document link to one of said documents as part of said response to said search query __wherein the contact center link is provided in addition to and separately from document links__.

3. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 2, further comprising the step of formatting said response to said search query to display a first result set including said document link and a second result set including said contact center link __wherein the second result set is dynamically generated based on contact center availability and resource allocation__.

4. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 1, wherein said data received in step (d) enable a plurality of contact center links to be provided to said user __corresponding to different contact center resources or skillsets selected based on the search query analysis__.

5. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 1, wherein said data received in step (d) comprise said contact center link __generated with embedded parameters specific to the user's search context__.

6. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 1, wherein said data received in step (d) comprise an identifier of a link cached by the search engine __wherein the identifier is associated with contact center resource availability information__.

7. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 1, wherein said contact center link is generated uniquely for said user __at the time of the search query response__, whereby activation of the link initiates an interactive communications session recognisable by the contact center as relating to said request from said search engine __and enables the contact center to retrieve the user's search context__.

8. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 1, wherein said request sent to said contact center includes an identifier of said user __and metadata describing the search query__, whereby a subsequent interactive communications session between the user and a resource of the contact center arising from initiation of said contact center link enables the contact center to associate said interactive communications session with said request from the search engine __and to provide contextually relevant assistance__.

9. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 8, wherein said identifier of said user is a network address of said user __and a session token generated by the search engine__.

10. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 1, wherein said contact center link when activated, initiates an interactive communications session between the user and a predetermined agent of the contact center selected in response to said request __based on agent skillset matching the search query topic__.

11. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 1, wherein said contact center link when activated, initiates an interactive communications session between the user and a predetermined queue of agents of the contact center selected in response to said request __wherein the queue is selected based on the search query classification__.

12. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 1, wherein said link is configured to initiate a communications session from a compatible communications application __installed on said user's computer__, if such application is available on said user's computer.

13. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 12, wherein said communications application is a voice or video telephony application __capable of receiving session parameters from the contact center link__.

17. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 1, wherein said contact center link contains parameters representing customer requirements __derived from the search query__ which are passed to said contact center within an interactive communications session initiated on activation of said contact center link.

18. (Original) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 1, wherein said parameters are indicative of one or more skillset parameters employed by a management system of said contact center, whereby said communications session may be directly assigned to a skillset based on the parameters.

19. (Currently Amended) A computer program product comprising a program carrier encoding instructions which, when executed by a search engine computer system, are effective to cause said search engine computer system to:
(a) provide a search engine interface to a user's computer system for searching documents on one or more websites;
(b) receive a search query from the user's computer system via said interface;
(c) send a request based on said search query to a computerised system of a contact center __that is distinct from the search engine system__;
(d) receive, in response to said request, data enabling a contact center link to be provided to said user, wherein said contact center link, when activated, initiates an interactive communications session between the user and a resource of the contact center __that is selected based on analysis of the search query content__; and
(e) return said contact center link to said user as part of a response to said search query __integrated with document search results__.

20. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented search engine system providing a user with access to a resource of a contact center, comprising:
(a) a server for providing a search engine interface to a user's computer system for searching documents on one or more websites and receiving a search query from the user's computer system via said interface;
(b) an interface for providing communication with a computerised system of a contact center __that is operationally separate from the search engine server__;
(c) a request generator for formulating a request based on said search query for sending to said computerised system of a contact center __that includes search context metadata__;
(d) a results generator for providing to said user a contact center link based on data received in response to said request, said contact center link being configured such that, when activated, it enables an interactive communications session between the user and a resource of the contact center __selected based on the search query analysis__.

21. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method of providing a user with access to a resource of a contact center, comprising the steps of:
(a) receiving from a search engine a request based on a search query submitted to the search engine by a user's computer system __wherein the request includes search context information__;
(b) determining, from said request, the identity of at least one selected resource of the contact center based on stored rules __that correlate search query topics to contact center resources__;
(c) sending to the search engine, in response to said request, data enabling a contact center link to be provided to said user, whereby said contact center link, when activated, will initiate an interactive communications session between the user and said selected resource of the contact center __wherein the link is generated with embedded session parameters__;
(d) receiving, from said user, a communications session initiation from which said selected resource may be identified __and the search context may be retrieved__; and
(e) directing said communications session to said selected resource __with the search context information__.

22. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 21, wherein said data comprise an address of said selected resource __and session parameters derived from the search query__, whereby activation of the link enables the user to initiate a communications session directly with said resource __with contextual information__.

23. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 21, wherein said data comprises an identification, for inclusion in a contact center link to be returned to the user, of one or more skillset parameters employed by a management system of said contact center __that match the search query topic__, whereby said communications session may be directly assigned to a skillset based on the parameters.

24. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 21, wherein said data comprises a unique identifier, for inclusion in a contact center link to be returned to the user, said unique identifier being assigned to said request received from said search engine __and generated at the time of the search query response__, whereby a later communications session may be associated with said request based on said unique identifier being communicated within said communications session __and enabling retrieval of search context__.

25. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 21, further comprising the step, carried out after having received a communications session initiation from the user, of amending the stored rules __to improve future resource selection__.

26. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 25, wherein the amendment of the stored rules confirms an association between the request received from the search engine __and the search query topic__ and the resource identified in a contact center link activated by the user.

27. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented method as claimed in claim 25, wherein the amendment of the stored rules confirms an association between the request received from the search engine __and the search query topic__ and a resource of the contact center which is different from that specified in a contact center link activated by the user but to which the user's communications session is ultimately directed.

28. (Currently Amended) A computer program product comprising a program carrier encoding instructions which, when executed by a computer system of a contact center, are effective to cause the computer system to:
(a) receive from a search engine a request based on a search query submitted to the search engine by a user's computer system __wherein the request includes search context information__;
(b) determine, from the request, the identity of at least one selected resource of the contact center based on stored rules __that correlate search query topics to contact center resources__;
(c) send to the search engine, in response to the request, data enabling a contact center link to be provided to the user, whereby the contact center link, when activated, will initiate an interactive communications session between the user and the selected resource of the contact center __wherein the link is generated with embedded session parameters__;
(d) receive, from the user, a communications session initiation from which the selected resource may be identified __and the search context may be retrieved__; and
(e) direct the communications session to the selected resource __with the search context information__.

29. (Currently Amended) A computer-implemented contact center system for providing users with access to a resource of a contact center system, comprising:
(a) an interface for receiving from a search engine a request based on a search query submitted to the search engine by a user's computer system __wherein the request includes search context metadata__ and for returning data to the search engine in response to the request;
(b) a storage area storing rules for determining, from the request, the identity of at least one selected resource of the contact center based on stored rules __that correlate search query topics to contact center resources and agent skillsets__;
(c) processing means programmed to determine the identity of at least one selected resource of the contact center based on the stored rules and to generate data enabling a contact center link to be provided to the user, whereby the contact center link, when activated, will initiate an interactive communications session between the user and the selected resource of the contact center __wherein the link is generated with embedded session parameters and search context information__;
wherein the processor is operably connected to the interface to receive the request therefrom and to provide the data thereto.
